/**
 * \page API API

Vector:
 - \c reduction1dVector : reduction of a vector in a scalar
 - \c exclusiveScan1dVector: prefix sum
 - \c dotProduct1dVector: dot product between two vectors
 - \c fftshift1dVector: fftshift operator on vector
 - \c normalizeVector: normalize vector by L1 norm
 - \c normL1Vector: L1 norm of a vector
 - \c normL2Vector: L2 norm of a vector
 - \c normLInfVector: L infinity norm of a vector

Dense Matrix:
 - \c reduction1dMatrix: reduction of a matrix non contiguous dimension into a vector
 - \c transposeMatrix: matrix transposition
 - \c gMatMul: general matrix-matrix multiplication (`C = alpha * A * B + beta * C`)
 - \c gMatVecMul: general matrix-vector multiplication
 - \c grad2dMatrix: gradient of a matrix
 - \c fliplr1dMatrix: flip elements in a matrix on one dimension
 - \c fftshift2dMatrix: fftshift operator on a matrix
 - \c dshear1dMatrix: dshear operator in a matrix on one dimension
 - \c downsample1dMatrix: downsample matrix on one dimension given a stride
 - \c convolution1dMatrix: convolution of multiple real signals in a matrix in frequency domain (half complex data layout)
 - \c correlation1dMatrix: correlation of multiple real signals in a matrix in frequency domain (half complex data layout)
 - \c convolutionReduction1dMatrix: convolution of multiple real signals in a matrix in frequency domain (half complex data layout) and 
 reduction of the results in a vector
 - \c convolutionTaperReduction1dMatrix: convolution of multiple real signals applying a spatial taper 
 in a matrix in frequency domain (half complex data layout) and reduction of the results in a vector
 - \c taper1dMatrix: apply different tapers on multiple 1d signals in a matrix
 - \c convolution2dMatrixDD: 2d convolution on a matrix in the data domain

Sparse Matrix:
 - \c gSpMatVecMulCSRVector : general sparse matrix-vector multiplication using CSR format and vector algorithm
 - \c gSpMatVecMulCSRAdaptive : general sparse matrix-vector multiplication using CSR format and adaptive algorithm
 - \c gSpMatVecMulELL : general sparse matrix-vector multiplication using ELL format

*/
